# Chapter 00 fixture/canonical separation — manual draft delta

Edited only `doc/migration/authored/migration/README.nepld` and `doc/migration/authored/guide/development.nepld`. Root-owned canonical Markdown, implementation, tests, registry and generated chapter 00 were not edited. No commit, runtime execution or canonical-on-main claim.

Read the current source diffs and authoring instructions before writing. Source and previous draft bytes are fixed in `before/`, with hashes/HEAD in `before.json`. Final drafts and hashes are in `after/` and `result.json`.

Migration README changes five prose paragraphs: registered Doc versus unregistered Markdown; the old converter's fixed pre-migration input and commit/digest receipt; the renamed converter-test fixture and unchanged generation command; no fixture-specific human review/anchor/cutover claim and separation from manually authored chapter zero; event comparison against the pre-migration fixture. Development changes one paragraph: per-OS fixed-fixture checks and Ubuntu artifact, with current-spec generation/checks explicitly on the separate `doc-canonical` route. Surrounding undeployed/general migration conditions remain unchanged.

Ordinary prose remains sentence literals. Paths and commands use explicit Sentence with InlineCode; the existing fixture link keeps its original typed relative target and full label. No new link or translation was invented. Kanji-only Ruby and okurigana are preserved, including 移行済/いこうず + み, 戻/もど + さず, 手書/てが + き, and 正式/せいしき + 第/だい + Text 0 + 章/しょう. The drafts refer to the parent directory's README as in the canonical source, without claiming this author independently reviewed its implementation provenance.

`check.py` passes for both complete Articles using the repository's formal-form structural parser, not the production runtime. All six changed paragraphs' base prose exactly matches the fixed Markdown paragraphs, apart from retaining the intended inline-code boundary space where Markdown line wrapping occurs. All existing RawCode bytes/hints, typed Link targets/labels, Section IDs/titles, List and Table structures are unchanged. New paths/code values and the `doc-canonical` operation name are exact. Source bytes remain unchanged. UTF-8 without BOM/LF and scoped `git diff --check` pass. The initial scratch checker shadowed its own helper function name, causing a TypeError; renaming its local variable resolved that checker error. It was not a draft or production failure.

This is author self-check; independent review and any actual parse/lower/HTML/rendered-link validation remain separate and unrun by this author.
